    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1034">

                <pb facs="1401" n="1391" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1391"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.1115/8–1545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-15T13:00:00-04:00">August 15, 1945—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1260. Dept. informed by Navy Dept that Naval forces operating in southern China
                    report recovery of American CIs<anchor n="13" xml:id="d1034-f1"/> and/or
                        POWs<anchor n="14" xml:id="d1034-f2"/> recently abandoned by Jap occupation
                    forces. Obtain from Am mil auth names of Am CIs now or later liberated and
                    telegraph names to Dept.</p>
                <p>In view current developments alert Consuls to necessity of obtaining and
                    transmitting info about liberated Am nationals. Invite Consuls’ attention to
                    Foreign Service Serial No. 353, April 17, 1945,<anchor n="15" xml:id="d1034-f3"
                    /> providing for emergency financial assistance loans to destitute Am
                    nationals.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1034-f1" n="13" xml:id="d1034-f1-content">
                <p>Civilian Internees.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1034-f2" n="14" xml:id="d1034-f2-content">
                <p>Prisoners of War.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1034-f3" n="15" xml:id="d1034-f3-content">
                <p>Circular Instruction to American Diplomtic and Consular Officers, “Emergency
                    Financial Assistance Loans to Destitute American Nationals in Foreign Countries
                    for Subsistence and Repatriation”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
